oe:use_calico_printing__doc_prussian_blue__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Prussian Blue used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. PRUSSIAN BLUE"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "For the mode of applying this pigment in dyeing, see CALICO-PRINTING. Sesquiferrocyanate of potash, is prepared by passing chlorine gas through a solution of ferrocyanide of potassium, till it becomes red, and ceases to precipitate the peroxide salts of iron."@en ;
