    oe:quoteText "LOGWOOD: a dye-wood used by the calico printer and others, obtained from the Hamatoxylon Campechianum, which affords the most durable deep red and black dye. Our imports have been on the increase of late years, and in 1856 we received about 89,000 tons."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 245" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n245> ;
