oe:use_calico_printing__0975__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Sulphuric Acid used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. SULPHATE OF MANGANESE"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "SULPHATE OF MANGANESE, is prepared on the great scale for the calico-printers, by exposing the peroxide of the metal and pitcoal ground together, and made into a paste with sulphuric acid, to a heat of 400° F."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. SULPHATE OF MANGANESE" ;
