oe:use_calico_printing__doc_oxalic_acid__q2 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Oxalic Acid used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 20"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "It is used by calico-printers, either pure or in the form of super-oxalate of potash, instead of citric acid; but the pure oxalic acid is apt to leave a stain on the linen, and the super-oxalate of potash is not sufficiently soluble in water to render the solution of a sufficient strength for many 10"@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 20" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n20/mode/1up> ;
