oe:use_calico_printing__doc_nitric_acid__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Nitric acid used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "The proportions of the acid mixture are the following:--1 gallon of water; and 1 gallon of nitric acid, of spec. grav. 1·288, which may be increased with the strength of the silk."@en ;
