    skos:editorialNote "Review decision (prune): Role corrected from the quote itself: catechu 'affords a fine permanent substantive brown' — a dye, not a mordant."@en .

oe:use_calico_printing__0275__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cutch used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "Catechu has been considerably employed by calico-printers of late years, as it affords a fine permanent substantive brown, of the shade called carmelite by the French."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F" ;
