    oe:quoteText "SAPAN-WOOD: a dye-wood obtained in Malabar, and the islands of the Eastern seas, from the Cesalpinia sappan, C. coriaria, and pulcherrima. A decoction of the wood is used by calico-printers for red dyes."@en ;
