    oe:quoteText "ANISE: The fruit of Pimpinilla anisum, under the name of aniseed, is principally imported from Alicant and Germany (the first is preferred), but some is also brought from the East Indies. It is an annual plant, largely cultivated in Spain, Malta, and various parts of Germany, and also in the island of Scio, Egypt, and parts of Asia. The imports are not large..."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section ANISE" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15191> ;
    oe:retrievalMode "direct_sentence" .

