    oe:quoteText "PITCH AND TAR MANUFACTURER: a maker of those commodities, largely used for smearing or covering ships' bottoms, palings, &c."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 302" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n302> ;
