oe:use_gunpowder_matches__doc_chlorate_of_potash__q2 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Chlorate of Potash used in Gunpowder, Explosives & Lucifer Matches: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. GUNPOWDER"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "When gunpowder is digested with chlorate of potash and dilute muriatic acid, at a moderate heat in a retort, the sulphur is acidified; but this process is disagreeable and slow, and consumes much chlorate."@en ;
