oe:use_hats_brushes_upholstery__doc_kapok__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Kapok used in Hat-Making, Brushes, Upholstery & Turnery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 224"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "KAPOK: a name, in the Eastern archipelago for the cotton down enveloping the seeds of the silk cotton-tree, Bombax pentandrum. It is used by the poor inhabitants for stuffing chairs, pillows, &c., but is seldom or never used for beds, it being thought unwholesome to sleep upon."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 224" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n224> ;
