oe:use_leather_tanning__0109__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Shumach used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 379"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "SUMACH: the dried and chopped leaves and shoots of the Rhus cortaria, a shrub growing in Southern Europe. When ground to powder in a mill, sumach is largely used for dyeing and tanning. The colouring matter is yellow. Our imports, average about 18,000 tons per annum."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 379" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n379> ;
