oe:use_leather_tanning__0072__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Galls used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. LEATHER"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "For the common purposes of the tanner, 1 pound of it would be equivalent also to 2-1/4 pounds of galls, to 7-1/2 of the Leicester willow, to 11 of the bark of the Spanish chesnut, to 18 of the bark of the common elm, to 21 of the bark of the common willow, and to 3 pounds of sumach."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. LEATHER" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    oe:retrievalMode "direct_sentence" .

oe:use_leather_tanning__0072__q2 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Galls used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section BARKS FOR TANNING"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "The bitter astringent bark and the galls of several of the Tamarisk tribe are also well suited for the purpose. Mesembryanthemum nodiflorum, one of the numerous indigenous species of the Cape, is used in making morocco leather."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section BARKS FOR TANNING" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/15191> ;
    oe:retrievalMode "direct_sentence" .

oe:use_leather_tanning__0072__q3 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Galls used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 48"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "Its principal use, however, is in the manufacture of sulphuric acid. Tannic Acid or Gallo-tannic Acid.—Tanning principle is contained in gall nuts of the Quercus infectoria, sumach, &c."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 48" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n48/mode/1up> ;
