oe:use_leather_tanning__0020__q2 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Hides Raw Dry used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. LEATHER"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "When calf skin is slowly tanned in weak solutions of the bark, or of catechu, it combines with a good deal of extractive matter, and though the increase of the weight of the skin be comparatively small, yet it has become perfectly insoluble in water, forming a soft, but at the same time a strong leather."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. LEATHER" ;
