    oe:quoteText "Soon after this, Edward, Lord Dudley, invented a process for smelting iron ore with pit-coal instead of timber; and it is difficult to point out many inventions that have been so advantageous."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 880" ;
