    oe:quoteText "BISMUTH: a reddish-white metal, occurring in brilliant plates, obtained chiefly in Saxony, and used as an alloy in type-metal and pewter. It is sometimes called by workmen tin-glass."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 50" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n50> ;
