oe:use_metallurgy_tinplate__doc_nitric_acid__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Nitric acid used in Metallurgy, Smelting, Brass & Tinplate: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. TIN MORDANTS"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "Place the tin-plate, slightly heated, over a tub of water, and rub its surface with a sponge dipped in a liquor composed of four parts of aquafortis, and two of distilled water, holding one part of common salt or sal ammoniac in solution."@en ;
