    oe:quoteText "LAT. Sal ammoniacum.) See AMMONIA. SAL PRUNELLA. This name is given to a salt composed of nitric acid, and potash; it may be obtained from common nitre, by fusing it in a crucible, so as to deprive it of some of its water, and nitric acid."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Mortimer (1823), General Commercial Dictionary, scan p. 883" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/generalcommercia00mort/page/n883/mode/1up> ;
