    oe:quoteText "PLUMBAGO: an emburet of iron commonly known as black lead, and also called graphite, used for making crucibles and leads for pencils; we import large quantities from Ceylon. A genus of plants with acrid, caustic properties. See LEAD-WORK."@en ;
