    oe:quoteText "ESPARTO: a name given in Spain to the herbaceous stalks of the Machrochlea (Stipa tenacissima), a grass which is used for mats, sandals, cordage, and for paper pulp."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 155" ;
