    rdfs:label "Evidence for Esparto and other Vegetable Fibres for making Paper used in Paper Making & Cardboard: Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 877"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "Moreover, as paper fibre, like esparto, must be fit for almost immediate immersion in the vats, paper-making can never pay the cost of separation and preparation, however simple and inexpensive."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Watt (1908), Commercial Products of India, scan p. 877" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n877/mode/1up> ;
    oe:retrievalMode "direct_sentence" .

