    oe:quoteText "STYRAX BENZOIN: The Benzoin Tree. The Resin = lubán (Ind. bazárs), hussí, shambiráni, kaminian, etc. A small tree of the Malay Archipelago, important as yielding the true Benzoin or Gum Benjamin of commerce. This substance appears to have been first mentioned by Ibn Batuta (Voy., etc., Fr. ed. 1858, iv., 228, 240), who visited Sumatra (A.D. 1325–49). He call..."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Sir George Watt, The Commercial Products of India (1908), scan p. 1064" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b31361584/page/n1064> ;
    oe:retrievalMode "direct_sentence" .

oe:use_perfumery_cosmetics__1599__q2 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Gum Benzoin used in Perfumery, Pomades & Essential Oils: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BENJAMIN"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "Benzoin is of great use in perfumery, as it enters into a number of preparations; among which may be mentioned fumigating pastilles, fumigating cloves (called also nails), poudre à la maréchale, &c."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BENJAMIN" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    oe:retrievalMode "direct_sentence" .

