    rdfs:label "Evidence for Lignum Quassia used in Pharmaceuticals & Druggists' Preparations: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 321"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "QUASSIA: a name for some bitter woods—the Surinam quassia is the produce of Quassia amara, and the Jamaican quassia of Picranea excelsa. They furnish a piro and simple bitter, and brewers are said to use the chips freely as a substitute for hops, although they have narcotic properties."@en ;
