    oe:quoteText "With certain vegetable oils, naphtha is said to form a good varnish.—2. Petroleum is much thicker than naphtha, resembling in consistence common tar."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 212" ;
