oe:use_woollen_silk_dyeing__0118__q1 a oe:EvidenceQuote ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cochineal used in Woollen, Silk & Worsted Dyeing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BRAZIL-WOOD"@en ;
    oe:quoteText "Brazil-wood is made use of for dyeing silk what is called false crimson, to distinguish it from the crimson made by means of cochineal, which is much more permanent."@en ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. BRAZIL-WOOD" ;
